# Project context

This is the **PRODATALYTICS** marketing site (`www.prodatalytics.com`): static HTML + Tailwind + vanilla JS on GitHub Pages. Not a React/Next app.

## Pages

| URL (typical) | File |
|---------------|------|
| `/` | `index.html` |
| `/pages/homepage.html` | Redirect stub to `/` (noindex) |
| `/pages/services.html` | Services + in-page anchors |
| `/pages/products.html` | Product accelerators (APIs, dashboards, toolkits) |
| `/pages/about.html` | Story / methodology |
| `/pages/contact.html` | FormSubmit + FAQ |
| `/pages/case-studies/` | Case study listing + detail pages |
| `/pages/insights/` | Articles (search) + newsletter signup |

RULE: keep `docs/SITE-MAP.md` in sync with every page, anchor, nav, JS or data-file change in the same edit (plus `sitemap.xml`, CODEBASE-INDEX, README tree). Never move/rename live pages without asking.
Full URL → file → owner map: `docs/SITE-MAP.md` (update it when adding pages; `npm run check` enforces).

## Source of truth

- Humans: `README.md`
- Agents: `AGENTS.md` + `.cursor/rules/`
- Styles: edit `css/tailwind.css` only; `css/main.css` is generated
- Shared behavior: `js/common.js`; contact-only: `js/contact.js`; insights: `js/insights.js` + `data/insights-index.json`
- Content briefs: `docs/content-templates.md`

## Content model

All copy is hardcoded in HTML. There is no CMS. Content changes = HTML edits, often duplicated across pages. New insight articles also need a row in `data/insights-index.json`.
